From f6bf9709d5fd9abe59a3e5316645e2382a5f7fde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukin <mylukin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Mar 2026 14:23:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 36/98] feat(feishu): use collapsible thinking panel in
 streaming cards

Separate thinking/tool status into a collapsible_panel, keeping the
main content element for streaming typewriter output. The thinking
panel is injected on-demand (first reasoning or tool event) and
collapsed when assistant text begins flowing.

Key changes:
- streaming-card: add updateThinking/collapseThinking, generic
  updateElementContent, buildFullElements with note preservation,
  thinkingInjected guard for retry on failed injection
- reply-dispatcher: route reasoning/tool updates to thinking panel,
  collapse on first partial reply, reset all per-cycle state in
  onReplyStart, implement shouldResetAfterTool (was dead code)
- streaming-card.test: fix pre-existing mock architecture (URL-aware
  fetchWithSsrFGuard, correct client.im.v1 path, pendingText field)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
